  "notes": [
    "Beverage Pairing: The rich, caramelized sweetness and savory butter notes pair exceptionally well with espresso, dark roast coffee, spiced chai, and earthy teas (like roasted hojicha or black tea), where the beverage's tannins balance the sweet crunch.",
    "How It Differs from Candied Pecans: Unlike standard candied or spiced pecans that typically rely on egg whites and sugar, butter toffee nuts are coated with real butter cooked to a hard-crack caramel stage, yielding a distinctly brittle, snappy shell and a deep dairy finish.",
    "Serving & Culinary Uses: Excellent for standalone snacking, but also easily chopped to garnish vanilla ice cream, warm morning oatmeal, baked goods, or added to a cheese and charcuterie board alongside sharp cheddar or aged cheeses.",
    "Storage Recommendation: Store in an airtight container in a cool, dry place away from heat and moisture to preserve the crisp, snappy texture of the toffee shell and prevent stickiness.",
    "Allergen Information: Contains tree nuts (pecans) and dairy (butter)."
  ],
